445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 199 0 R
/E (Modern retail businesses manage thousands of daily transactions across sales, inventory, purchasing, and administrative operations, often resulting in stock discrepancies, billing errors, inefficient inventory tracking, and limited financial visibility. The primary objective of this project is to design, implement, and validate a centralized Retail Inventory and Sales Management System using a Relational Database Management System \(RDBMS\) integrated with an interactive web application. The system architecture is structured around relational database principles, incorporating entities such as users, products, categories, suppliers, sales, sale items, purchases, stock movements, and audit logs. The database is designed using normalization principles up to Third Normal Form \(3NF\) to minimize data redundancy and maintain consistency. MySQL enforces primary key and foreign key constraints, while transaction management ensures reliable sales processing, accurate stock deductions, and consistent purchase records. The application provides role-based access for administrators, cashiers, and inventory managers, along with product management, point-of-sale billing, purchase recording, low-stock monitoring, sales reporting, and inventory tracking. Comprehensive testing focuses on data integrity, transactional consistency, access control, and the accuracy of inventory and sales operations. The completed application serves as a practical and extensible prototype for improving retail operational efficiency, maintaining accurate stock records, and supporting data-driven business decisions.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
