455 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (This chapter presents the operational challenges, project objectives, system boundaries, architectural strategy, functional requirements, and conceptual Entity-Relationship design developed for the Retail Inventory and Sales Management System. It outlines how a centralized relational database and an interactive web application can address common retail management challenges, including inventory discrepancies, billing inaccuracies, inefficient purchase tracking, and limited sales visibility. The chapter also establishes the system architecture, defines the responsibilities of administrators, cashiers, and inventory managers, and introduces the database structure designed to ensure data integrity, consistency, and efficient retail operations.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 200 0 R
/E (Modern retail operations involve highly interconnected business workflows, including product registration, category management, supplier record maintenance, purchase order processing, point-of-sale billing, inventory updates, stock movement tracking, and sales report generation. In traditional paper-based stores or decentralized spreadsheet systems, records are often maintained separately across billing, inventory, and administrative functions. This fragmentation creates significant operational problems, including inaccurate stock quantities, duplicate or inconsistent product records, billing errors, inefficient purchase tracking, and delays in identifying low-stock items. Sales and inventory records may become inconsistent when stock deductions are not properly synchronized with completed transactions. Furthermore, limited coordination between purchasing and sales operations can lead to stock shortages, excess inventory, and difficulties reconciling revenue with recorded transactions. These challenges highlight the need for a centralized Retail Inventory and Sales Management System that integrates essential retail workflows, maintains reliable database relationships, and improves operational transparency through accurate, consistent, and accessible information.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
