/Title (2. Second Normal Form \(2NF\) Compliance: Relations with composite candidate keys were evaluated to ensure every non-prime attribute is fully functionally dependent on the entire primary key. In test management, diagnostic metadata \($test\\_name, standard\\_cost$\) was isolated into lab_tests, avoiding partial dependencies on consultation order keys.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5612 0 R
/Prev 5630 0 R
/Next 5638 0 R
>>
endobj
5638 0 obj
<<
/Title (3. Third Normal Form \(3NF\) Compliance: All transitive dependencies \($X ightarrow Y ightarrow Z$\) where $X$ is a candidate key and $Y$ is a non-prime attribute were eliminated. For example, in doctors, department location \($building\\_block$\) was not stored directly; instead, dept_id acts as a foreign key determinant to departments. In beds, ward properties \($ward\\_type, capacity$\) are resolved via ward_id. Consequently, for every non-trivial functional dependency $X ightarrow Y$, $X$ is a superkey, satisfying 3NF.)
/Dest [29 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5612 0 R
/Prev 5637 0 R
/Next 5631 0 R
>>
endobj
